{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1240363-court-bargains-with-entities","id":1240363,"title":"Court Bargains With Entities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-30T02:13:02-07:00","id":1240363,"title":"Court Bargains With Entities","content":"Hey so i was reading through the custuomizing your own chronicle section in the new book, right? So what i found interesting was the section on Bargains prospective courts can make with Entities, Emotions and Concepts. What i was taking note of was entities((the first example of it was this Atomic Clock in Prague which got fed disquiet-turned glamour), what other entities material and spiritual would be powerful enough to make a court bargain? I mean it is easy to imagine god level entities like rank 6+ ephemerals and things like the God-Machine, The Dark Mother and the Principle could fit the bill. I was pondering about less obvious options, therefore i wanted you guyses take on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T12:00:59-07:00","id":1240536,"title":"","content":"So, <i>not</i> cosmic representations of things? More prosaic beings like the Spirits of Cities, powerful Geists, Ancient Vampires, etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:14:09-07:00","id":1240581,"title":"","content":"Given the amount of time Changelings spend in Dreams I think powerful Goetia from the Temenos or even entities from the Anima Mundi would be the most appropriate for such Court Bargains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T14:37:57-07:00","id":1240590,"title":"","content":"Lately I've been constructing a court whose patron entity is a bullet-train hydra (appropriately, the Court of the Hydra-Line), a very recent court started by a Changeling who escaped from Arcadia when their Keeper tried to forcibly incorporate said bullet-train hydra into its realm. It failed, rather miserably, and the Changeling managed to form a rapport with the hydra. Eventually, he managed to convince it to share its power in exchange for its own form of worship, leading it to growing and the court itself solidifying.<br /> <br /> As for what the hydra is, I'm pondering on it either being a powerful Hob, a Horror that lives in the Hedge, or perhaps something else that simply was picked up by the Gentry and it adapted to the Hedge. What I'm working off of is the idea that the court doesn't just gain power from the Patron itself, but their actions also work to empower it too. Worship, glamour and general actions that enforce its power, which in turn empowers its followers into worshiping it easier.<br /> <br /> I'm still working on the Bargain itself, but I've got a few contracts and the mantle already written up.<br /> <br /> This whole court was inspired by this: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AKSz-BarF2Y\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AKSz-BarF2Y</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T15:22:13-07:00","id":1240607,"title":"","content":"they can bargain directly with cosmic forces/concept too, but also with singular entities. The only criteria is that they have to be powerful enough to make bargains with a court and benefit from it in turn. Or rather empowers the court's coping strategies and is empowered by them in return. So i was pondering if i in theory could homebrew a court of changelings serving as a mummy's cult or one connected to a powerful beast or vampire and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:50:03-07:00","id":1240655,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure a Beast Incarnate would work as a Patron. They definitely acquire a ton of physical and metaphysical potency on the journey there, as well as an understanding of narratives and the subverting thereof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:03:07-07:00","id":1240923,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a Mummy would work as a Patron for a Court of Changelings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:40:22-07:00","id":1240941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1240363-court-bargains-with-entities?p=1240923#post1240923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if a Mummy would work as a Patron for a Court of Changelings</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I can't think of why they wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Also the idea of motley/freehold-cults is an...interesting one to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T11:14:33-07:00","id":1240964,"title":"","content":"I would say no to a Mummy, for the same reason a Demon, an Archmage or even a Beast Incarnate wouldn't work; they're not only too small of a source, but innevitably they're not going to stick around to freely offer up that level of protection, especially if the Court is to catch on in other Freeholds. The entities that grant protection are grant, inhuman and connected to power in a way that the playale splats simply aren't. In a sense, they are storytelling devices. A Mummy, a Beast Incarnate, an Archmage? They are all singular units with their own statistics, a limited pool of disparate powers and, innevitably, will have a fall from grace and into death.<br /> <br /> Now, if you were to make a Bargain with the forces that allow Mummies to come back, or the very embodiment of Demonic Primum, or the Watchtowers (even if that is <i>highly</i> unlikely) or even the Dark Mother herself? That's a source.<br /> <br /> But this all does rely on ST fiat, so if you want to do it that way, then go for it. Just remember, Mummies do slumber and I doubt the court would have its power when it is doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T11:29:31-07:00","id":1240972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1240363-court-bargains-with-entities?p=1240964#post1240964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say no to a Mummy, for the same reason a Demon, an Archmage or even a Beast Incarnate wouldn't work; they're not only too small of a source, but innevitably they're not going to stick around to freely offer up that level of protection, especially if the Court is to catch on in other Freeholds. The entities that grant protection are grant, inhuman and connected to power in a way that the playale splats simply aren't. In a sense, they are storytelling devices. A Mummy, a Beast Incarnate, an Archmage? They are all singular units with their own statistics, a limited pool of disparate powers and, innevitably, will have a fall from grace and into death.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Courts of the Grey City Freehold are collectively hitched to what is either the aggregate will of a collection of stolen Fae Regalia, a noble Title exclusive to hobgoblins, a toll-road out of Arcadia, a city-eidolon, a single weird urban legend, a falling angel and its demonic antecedent, or a fae-adjacent chunk of the American Dream.<br /> <br /> Neither of them conducts their activities outside of the Loop of Chicago and its neighboring supernatural environs and I would be remiss if I didn't say there are probably multiple individual entities that have wider reach and greater power than that, but that doesn't matter: a Court's Bargain requires only that the other party be strong enough to intercede in some fashion and is part of a metaphysical framework built into the principle of exchange \u2014 the attendant Courtly rituals changelings conduct as part of their Bargain with an entity may well enhance its ability and willingness to serve as a patron, and there are some big honking levers for that to be relevant for all of the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T11:50:23-07:00","id":1240979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1240363-court-bargains-with-entities?p=1240972#post1240972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Courts of the Grey City Freehold are collectively hitched to what is either the aggregate will of a collection of stolen Fae Regalia, a noble Title exclusive to hobgoblins, a toll-road out of Arcadia, a city-eidolon, a single weird urban legend, a falling angel and its demonic antecedent, or a fae-adjacent chunk of the American Dream.<br /> <br /> Neither of them conducts their activities outside of the Loop of Chicago and its neighboring supernatural environs and I would be remiss if I didn't say there are probably multiple individual entities that have wider reach and greater power than that, but that doesn't matter: a Court's Bargain requires only that the other party be strong enough to intercede in some fashion and is part of a metaphysical framework built into the principle of exchange \u2014 the attendant Courtly rituals changelings conduct as part of their Bargain with an entity may well enhance its ability and willingness to serve as a patron, and there are some big honking levers for that to be relevant for all of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>I shall defer to your expertise then Satchel. I still feel a playable splat isn't a good idea for a Bargain patron, but it it makes a good a good story, then why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T12:15:46-07:00","id":1240984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1240363-court-bargains-with-entities?p=1240979#post1240979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still feel a playable splat isn't a good idea for a Bargain patron, but it it makes a good a good story, then why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth remembering: fae little-b &quot;bargains&quot; operate on similar constraints, and the workarounds for changelings are equally applicable to the patron of a Bargain as a means of upholding their end of the deal \u2014 the Apex of a Begotten hive very likely has the social capital to support a Court by mere virtue of knowing the right monsters, and the Unchained can make a Pactbound the core of a cult through simple magical documentation, to say nothing of the occult backing Seekers and Arisen have to offer.<br /> <br /> Singular Prometheans and lone werewolves are more likely out of the running, but if you have the reach to keep your word then you have the power to make a Bargain. It might not necessarily be a very <i>potent</i> Bargain in terms of what it offers to changelings vis-a-vis keeping the Fae and their agents from hassling you, but as a narrative basis for Contracts and Mantles it's entirely in keeping with the metaphysics that a pact with Merlin Hookhand Imhotep gives a group of changelings more options for their magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T12:32:12-07:00","id":1240989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1240363-court-bargains-with-entities?p=1240923#post1240923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if a Mummy would work as a Patron for a Court of Changelings</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't figured out the particulars of it yet, but Sleeping Lions has a deal with an henet of three Arisen as it's cornerstone-they are the jinn to keep in the bottle, so to speak. ANd of course, THe Forest of Teeth is all about the weirdness that coems from the transmutations bwteen the Wyrd and spiritual resonance, with at least one Court-Lodge being backed by a spirit.<br /> <br /> Having the other splats work as the basis for courts/freeholds depends on how they're metaphysics works and the load born on them directly versus them as a conduit as well as some clear ideas of how, but I feel like the door is open to allow for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T13:42:33-07:00","id":1241009,"title":"","content":"Archmasters are capable of retroactively rewriting reality and are only technically playable characters and operate at the same level as rank 6+ entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T01:49:59-07:00","id":1241203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1240363-court-bargains-with-entities?p=1240590#post1240590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what the hydra is, I'm pondering on it either being a powerful Hob, a Horror that lives in the Hedge, or perhaps something else that simply was picked up by the Gentry and it adapted to the Hedge. What I'm working off of is the idea that the court doesn't just gain power from the Patron itself, but their actions also work to empower it too. Worship, glamour and general actions that enforce its power, which in turn empowers its followers into worshiping it easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>literally</i> say Incarnate Begotten - or are least Unfettered - with being mythical being, invading dreams and being empowered and fed by actions of it's cultists. With being a Hydra, Begotten after Inheritance is closest you can have to perfect much in <b>CoD</b> universe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:20:20-07:00","id":1241251,"title":"","content":"I mean the Begotten in general can make primordial cults to empower them further","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:35:32-07:00","id":1241588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1240363-court-bargains-with-entities?p=1241203#post1241203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It <i>literally</i> say Incarnate Begotten - or are least Unfettered - with being mythical being, invading dreams and being empowered and fed by actions of it's cultists. With being a Hydra, Begotten after Inheritance is closest you can have to perfect much in <b>CoD</b> universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of options for a Hydra not related to the playable splats. I actually had a thought of a Bullet Train Horror from the mundane world in a scrapyard. A homeless person there gets taken by a Gentry, but when the Horror rears up the Gentry takes notice, and takes it to Arcadia. Of course, the travel through the Hedge and exposure to the fae magic is enough to give it a proper awakening, and empowerment, and it escapes. Alternatively, it could be an Eidolon literally from a dream that a Changeling, Gentry or Huntsman removed, which took on a life of its own. It could even be a toy train that marinated for too long, came alive, and kept growing until it is what it is when the founder of the court finds and makes a bargain with it.<br /> <br /> I also hesitate to use an Incarnate Beast because, simply put, once the Beast falls from its Apex Predator position, it comes away weaker than before given that anyone can place an anathema on it and without any of its Incarnate abilities. This is up to ST fiat, and it could work well for the court to help keep their Patron on top of their game, but it's still something to consider.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T18:02:15-07:00","id":1241598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div c